lavender: kernel log over USB, WinUSB (no driver needed on Windows)

- bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c rewritten for SDM660: DWC3 at 0x0a800000, one vendor interface with
  Microsoft OS 2.0 descriptors, bulk IN carries the console log ring from the first boot
  message, bulk OUT takes text commands: lv:ping, lv:reset, lv:fastboot (PM660 restart
  reason over the SPMI arbiter, then a warm PS_HOLD reset)
- started from the platform expert, so it does not depend on a storage driver
- boot-arg lvusb=0 turns it off
- the source is generated: xnu/src/gen_usb.py + sweet_usb.c.in (USB descriptors are built there)

